.Sh CAVEATS
The staging buffer of every handle and
.Fa buf Ns .mem
must not be
.Dv nullptr ,
even for zero-length writes; this is assumed, not checked.
A writer's
.Fa buffer Ns .size
must not be zero.
.Pp
Interrupted or failed system calls are not retried.
After an fs writer fails, some bytes may already have been written while
.Fa end
is unchanged, so flushing again can write them twice.
After
.Fn xft_read_from_reader
fails,
.Pf * Fa total
is not set and bytes already copied to
.Fa dst
are consumed from the reader.
.Pp
The raw drain path tests its capacity check with the wrong sense:
when a write overflows the staging buffer,
.Fn xft_writer_write
on a raw writer returns
.Dv KO
if
.Fa external
has room, and copies past the end of
.Fa external
if it does not.
Writes that fit in the staging buffer and
.Fn xft_writer_flush
are not affected.
.Pp
Do not pass the zeroed result of a failed
.Fn xft_map_file
to
.Fn xft_unmap_file .
.Pp
.Fn xft_get_fs_reader
is declared
.Ql always_inline
in
.In io.h
without a body, so compilers that honor the attribute strictly, such as GCC
without LTO, reject calls to it from outside the library.
